    "trigger": "User taps info icon (i) next to Cardio Fitness Score on the Health & Wellness screen",
    "title": "Cardio Fitness Score & VO2 Max: The Single Strongest Predictor of Healthspan",
    "description": "What your estimated maximal oxygen uptake (VO2 Max) reveals about cardiopulmonary efficiency and all-cause mortality risk.",
    "content": "### 1. What is VO2 Max?\nCardio Fitness Score is a clinical estimation of your **VO2 Max**—the maximum volume of oxygen (in milliliters) that your body can transport and metabolize per kilogram of body weight in one minute ($\\text{mL/kg/min}$). It serves as the definitive physiological benchmark of cardiovascular, pulmonary, and mitochondrial conditioning.\n\n### 2. The Fick Principle: The Biology of Oxygen Delivery\nVO2 Max is dictated by the Fick Equation:\n$$\\text{VO}_2 = Q \\times (a - v)\\text{O}_2$$\nWhere $Q$ is maximal cardiac output (the volume of blood your heart can pump) and $(a - v)\\text{O}_2$ is the arteriovenous oxygen difference (the amount of oxygen extracted from arterial blood by peripheral muscle mitochondria).\n\n### 3. The Ultimate Longevity Biomarker\nIn epidemiological studies published by the Cleveland Clinic and the American Heart Association, cardiorespiratory fitness demonstrated a stronger association with all-cause mortality than smoking, diabetes, or hypertension:\n- Moving from the 'Low' category to the 'Below Average' category reduces mortality risk by 50%.\n- Individuals in the 'Elite' category exhibit up to a 5-fold reduction in cardiovascular mortality compared to those with low aerobic fitness.\n\n### 4. How to Improve Your Score\n1. **The Base:** Accumulate 150+ minutes of weekly Zone 2 cardio to expand mitochondrial density.\n2. **The Peak:** Incorporate one session of **4x4 Norwegian Interval Training** weekly (4 minutes at 90%–95% HR Max, followed by 3 minutes of active recovery, repeated 4 times).",
    "takeaway": "Higher Cardio Fitness / VO2 Max correlates directly with lower cardiovascular mortality; regular interval training and Zone 2 work are the twin pillars to elevate it.",
    "reading_time": "3 min",
    "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1538805060514-97d9cc17730c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",
