    "trigger": "User taps info icon (i) next to the Cycle Phase indicator on the Cycle screen",
    "title": "The Four Menstrual Phases: Hormonal Drivers of Energy, Mood, and Metabolism",
    "description": "How the 28-day ebb and flow of Estrogen and Progesterone governs your energy, insulin sensitivity, and athletic performance.",
    "content": "### 1. The Infradian Rhythm: The 28-Day Biological Clock\nWhile male biology operates almost exclusively on a 24-hour circadian clock, female physiology is additionally governed by a 28-day **Infradian Rhythm**. This monthly hormonal cycle orchestrates body temperature, resting heart rate, glucose tolerance, and metabolic recovery.\n\n### 2. Breakdown of the Four Hormonal Phases\n1. **Menstrual Phase (Days 1–5):**\n   - *Hormonal Profile:* Both estrogen and progesterone hit rock bottom. The thickened endometrium is shed.\n   - *Physiological State:* Energy stores are conserved. Systemic inflammation may be slightly elevated due to uterine prostaglandins. Focus on gentle movement and restorative rest.\n2. **Follicular Phase (Days 6–13):**\n   - *Hormonal Profile:* The pituitary gland releases Follicle-Stimulating Hormone (FSH). Ovarian follicles mature, driving a sharp exponential rise in **Estrogen** (estradiol).\n   - *Physiological State:* Estrogen increases insulin sensitivity, accelerates muscle protein synthesis, and elevates dopamine and serotonin. This is your peak window for strength gains and mental sharpness.\n3. **Ovulatory Phase (Around Day 14):**\n   - *Hormonal Profile:* Estrogen peaks, triggering a surge of Luteinizing Hormone (LH) that causes the dominant follicle to rupture and release an egg. Testosterone reaches its monthly crest.\n   - *Physiological State:* Maximal physical power, athletic stamina, and peak libido.\n4. **Luteal Phase (Days 15–28):**\n   - *Hormonal Profile:* The collapsed follicle forms the *corpus luteum*, which secretes large quantities of **Progesterone**.\n   - *Physiological State:* Progesterone raises core resting temperature by $0.3^\\circ\\text{C}$ to $0.5^\\circ\\text{C}$ and accelerates resting heart rate. Protein catabolism increases, sleep architecture becomes more fragmented, and carbohydrate cravings rise prior to menses.",
    "takeaway": "Female physiology operates on a 28-day infradian rhythm; aligning your workouts and nutrition with your hormonal shifts prevents burnout and maximizes strength.",
    "reading_time": "3 min",
    "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518611012118-696072aa579a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",
    "source_name": "Flo Health",
    "source_url": "https://flo.health/menstrual-cycle/health/menstrual-cycle-phases",
    "hero_image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518611012118-696072aa579a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",
    "inline_image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1508214751196-bcfd4ca60f91?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80",
    "inline_caption": "The four distinct endocrine phases: Menstrual, Follicular, Ovulatory, and Luteal."
