    "trigger": "User taps info icon (i) next to the Cervical Fluid logging field on the Cycle screen",
    "title": "Cervical Fluid 101: Decoding Vaginal Discharge as an Estrogen Mirror",
    "description": "How the physical consistency, pH, and elasticity of cervical mucus shift across the cycle to protect or facilitate sperm motility.",
    "content": "### 1. What is Cervical Fluid?\nCervical fluid (or cervical mucus) is a dynamic biological hydrogel secreted by specialized crypt glands inside the cervix. Far from being random discharge, its volume, viscosity, and chemical composition are regulated directly by circulating levels of estrogen and progesterone.\n\n### 2. The Four Primary Consistencies Across the Cycle\n1. **Dry or Sticky (Post-Menses / Early Follicular):**\n   - *Hormone Driver:* Low estrogen, baseline progesterone.\n   - *Appearance:* Minimal fluid; feels tacky, pasty, or rubbery.\n   - *Fertility Status:* Low. The mucus forms a dense, acidic physical barrier that prevents sperm penetration.\n2. **Creamy (Mid-Follicular):**\n   - *Hormone Driver:* Rising estrogen.\n   - *Appearance:* Milky white or pale yellow, resembling hand lotion or yogurt.\n   - *Fertility Status:* Moderate. Fluid volume is expanding, transitioning toward an alkaline pH.\n3. **Egg-White / Stretchy (Peak Fertile Window / Ovulation):**\n   - *Hormone Driver:* Peak estrogen (estradiol).\n   - *Appearance:* Completely clear, wet, slippery, and elastic (known clinically as *spinnbarkeit*), stretching several inches between thumb and index finger like raw egg white.\n   - *Fertility Status:* **Peak Fertility.** This hydrogel forms microscopic parallel swimming channels that filter, nourish, and transport sperm into the uterine cavity.\n4. **Tacky or Dry (Luteal Phase):**\n   - *Hormone Driver:* Dominant progesterone.\n   - *Appearance:* Quickly turns cloudy, thick, and viscous, sealing off the cervical canal post-ovulation.",
    "takeaway": "Stretchy, clear, egg-white cervical fluid indicates peak estrogen levels and confirms you have entered your most fertile days.",
    "reading_time": "3 min",
    "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1508214751196-bcfd4ca60f91?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",
